  "confidence": 0.7,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "short_to_ground",
      "components": ["R12", "T5", "T4"],
      "pins": ["R12.2", "T5.1", "T4.3"],
      "nets": ["T4.3/T5.1 gate node", "GND"],
      "observed": "In the ATO Valve driver, R12 (10 k) ties the gate of the low-side N-MOSFET T5 (AO3400A) / collector of the NPN level-shifter T4 (BT3904) down to GND, and there is no pull-up to +3V3 on that node. The structurally identical Main Pump driver instead uses R5 (10 k) as a pull-up from +3V3 to its T2 gate / T1 collector node.",
      "expected": "For a common-emitter NPN level-shifter driving an N-MOS low-side switch, the collector/gate node must be pulled up to the logic rail (here +3V3, as R5 does for the main pump) so the MOSFET gate can be raised above Vth. A pull-down to GND leaves the gate at 0 V whether T4 is off or on, so T5 can never turn on.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "ATO Valve: R12 10k between T5 gate / T4 collector node and GND (no +3V3 on that node); Main Pump: R5 10k between +3V3 and T2 gate / T1 collector node"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "T3 — AON6407 (8-DFN N-MOSFET) | ATO solenoid-valve low-side switch ... gate driven through R10 (100 Ω), pre-driven via T4 (BT3904)."}
      ],
      "impact": "The ATO solenoid valve never energizes: automatic top-off and the high-level overflow shut-off via the valve are dead, so the reservoir can run dry or overflow.",
      "confidence": 0.7
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["PR1", "H1"],
      "pins": ["PR1.5", "PR1.2", "PR1.3", "PR1.1"],
      "nets": ["EZO_PDIS", "I2C_SDA", "I2C_SCL", "+5V"],
      "observed": "The TF-Luna LiDAR PR1 is wired through header H1 to +5V, I2C_SDA, I2C_SCL and GND, and its TX pin is joined to the EZO_PDIS net (the ADM3260 isolator power-disable control).",
      "expected": "Per the specification, PR1 is not implemented in this revision: its pins are typed 'free', it is marked on_board:no / excluded, and it must not connect to any net. EZO_PDIS should drive only U3.8 and U4.8.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Water Height Sensor: PR1 LiDAR VCC/SDA/SCL/GND/TX/RX wired to H1, with H1 carrying +5V, I2C_SDA, I2C_SCL, GND and EZO_PDIS"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "the r2 netlist shows PR1 with on_board: no ... all four pins (VCC, SDA, SCL, GND) typed free — i.e., it is not connected to any net in this design."}
      ],
      "impact": "If PR1 is populated, the isolator power-disable line EZO_PDIS is bridged to the LiDAR TX and the main I2C bus is loaded by an unintended device, conflicting with the documented isolated-EZO control scheme.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The drawing deviates from the intended design in two places: the ATO-valve low-side switch has its gate-bias resistor R12 tied to GND instead of pulled up to +3V3 (unlike the identical main-pump driver's R5), so the valve MOSFET can never turn on and automatic top-off fails; and the TF-Luna LiDAR PR1, which the spec states is unwired/free, is in fact connected to the I2C/+5V nets and has its TX bridged to the EZO_PDIS control line."
}

